# Python packages for the media capture (scripts/capture-media.sh): Pillow
# assembles the GIFs. `requirements.txt` is the hashed lock compiled from this
# file, and the capture script installs it with `--require-hashes`, so what runs
# in the media workflow is exactly what was reviewed. Regenerate after editing:
#
#   uv pip compile --universal --generate-hashes --python-version 3.10 \
#       scripts/media/requirements.in -o scripts/media/requirements.txt
Pillow>=11,<13
